WEBVTT

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:14.450
Soshukan Private High School

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:14.450
Wednesday, May 4th

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:14.450
6:56 PM

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.600
Found ya!

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.010
<b><i>Backflip!!</i></b>

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:46.270
Thirty Minutes Earlier

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.170
You boys really applied yourselves.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.960
The training camp is officially over.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.060
Good work, everyone.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.860
To the members of Ao High,

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.310
I'm looking forward to facing you 
at the Tohoku Regional Tournament.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.320
Assuming you make it through prefecturals.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.800
Right back at you.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.040
Don't get cocky and 
muck it up, Aomorillapple.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.560
What was that, you sasakama sucker?!

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.500
Both of you, please calm down.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.380
Want me to lay him out, Captain?

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.420
Please stay out of this, Watari.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:17.040
Camp's over already? This stinks.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.670
You want to practice a little more, Mashiro?

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.630
I can do without the practice, but...

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.510
Hey! Watch your tone around your senpai!

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.750
They're always this way. Just let them be.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.470
You're always saying that crap!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:27.470
Yah!

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.600
Please calm down, you two!

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:30.880
It's just no fun...

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.270
Do as you're told for once! Hey!

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:32.390
Enough!

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:33.580
Yes, sir!

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.620
I suppose it <i>is</i> a little early.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.070
We should have prepared 
an additional activity.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.740
Perhaps a light game of some kind?

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:44.030
I know! Hide-and-seek!

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:45.760
Hide-and-seek?!

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.500
But not just any hide-and-seek!

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.380
<i>Double-it</i> hide-and-seek!

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:52.410
We pick one "it" from each school,

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.520
then compete to see 
who finds the most people!

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.280
What do you think we are, little kids?

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.480
So we compete? I see...

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:05.020
I can't back down from a competition.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.510
All right! You're on!

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.450
Are we really?

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:09.770
Yay!

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.980
C-Coach?

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.930
The coach's dark side...

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:15.340
It's on full display.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.800
Oh, so he's <i>that</i> kind of guy?

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.400
He is indeed that type.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:23.510
Can we still use the gym?

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:27.870
The school closes at eight, 
 so we can stay inside until then.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.410
Then let's use the whole school!

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.290
But we need to be out by eight, okay?

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:35.830
That means we have an hour and a half.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:37.580
Let's decide who's "it"!

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.170
Ready, and...

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:40.750
Rock, paper...

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.400
Found ya!

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.560
Nobody here...

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.060
Nobody here, either.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.060
Damn. Where the hell're they hidin'?

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:54.620
Wanna head downstairs?

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:55.870
S-Sure.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:59.820
That was close!

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.640
You don't need to be scared—

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:08.680
Must be hearin' things.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.310
Misato-kun, you're here, too?

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:15.410
Thank goodness our captains 
are so oblivious.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.600
I see. The library, eh?

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:22.540
I can't imagine they'd be 
eager to pay this place a visit.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.560
With those two doing the seeking,

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:27.340
I expect we'll spend a lot of time hiding.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.060
Heya!

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:34.950
Hey.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.600
Oh, I'm not the first one here.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:39.960
Hey.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.820
Our captain's kind of a simpleton.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.320
I suspect yours is, too.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:51.180
Then we have a long, 
boring wait ahead of us.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:04.950
The safest course might be 
to stay on the move.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.430
<i>This is kind of awkward.</i>

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:21.350
<i>Come to think of it, I've never 
really been alone with Misato-kun.</i>

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:23.910
<i>He always leaves right after practice.</i>

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:28.000
<i>Wait, could this be... 
our chance to get closer?</i>

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:31.120
S-So, Misato-kun...

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.770
M-My family's from Sendai.

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:38.180
Where's yours from again?

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:39.090
Natori.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:42.010
Wow, really?

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:44.010
How long have you been 
doing rhythmic gymnastics?

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:45.270
Since elementary school.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:46.250
Wow...

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.830
<i>All right! This is going great!</i>

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:50.750
So you had a rhythmic
 gymnastics team at your school?

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:53.120
No, a local sports club.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.220
What made you want to take it up?

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.420
<i>No answer?</i>

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:06.170
<i>Did I ask something wrong?!</i>

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:08.470
<i>Wh-Wh-What was it? Where'd I mess up?</i>

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:09.990
<i>Um, what'd I ask him again?</i>

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:13.240
<i>Where he's from, when he 
started gymnastics, and then...</i>

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.410
<i>Um...</i>

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:17.760
Misa-pon was really awesome!

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:18.800
Mashiro!

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:19.280
When did you get here?!

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:20.000
Just now!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.200
I got bored hiding all by myself.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.690
You're the one who wanted 
to play hide-and-seek—

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:27.540
Now, if you wanna know 
how awesome Misa-pon was...

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:28.760
Are you even listening?

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.660
After the move to Natori 
in the last year of junior high...

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.170
Misato-kun, you were a transfer student?

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:34.800
He's talking about himself.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.620
He transferred to my school in our third year

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.350
and came to watch our team practice.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.100
Yep! And that's where...

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:50.310
Mashiro-kun, you'd never done 
rhythmic gymnastics before then?

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:51.240
Nope!

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:54.830
And you became the individuals 
champion so soon after starting?

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:57.650
Well, Misa-pon was the only
 decent competition there.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:59.140
Right, Misa-pon?

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:03.230
Why can't I find 
a single freakin' one of 'em?

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:04.660
By the way, Takase...

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:05.890
Wh-What?

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:07.740
Why do you keep taggin' along with me?

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:09.880
It ain't much of a competition like this.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:15.730
You have a home turf advantage here.

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:18.800
I intended to prey on that...

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:22.020
But it seems even hide-and-seek is too much

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:24.310
for a plebeian who can't appreciate apples.

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:28.600
Says the guy too dumb to recognize 
the greatness of sasakama!

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.880
H-Hey, wait up!

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:33.130
Still, I must say that those captains 
of ours are quite a handful.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:34.440
You're telling me.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:37.200
They really got off on 
the wrong foot two years ago...

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:39.420
What's all this?

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:43.700
Each school brought 
a local delicacy for the joint practice.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.490
The apples were our contribution.

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:48.170
Wait, apples?

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.650
Who brought these?

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:50.710
Aomori.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.530
I hear it was Shiro High.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:55.470
Whatever. Apples taste the same 
no matter where they're from.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:09:00.030
So this is sasa kamaboko, huh?

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:01.230
I wonder if it's good.

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:05.390
Meh! It's just boring old kamaboko 
with a different shape, I bet.

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:09.980
"Boring old kamaboko"?!

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:12.360
"All apples taste the same"?!

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:17.470
Your backflips are as bland as your apples!

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:18.410
What was that?!

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:22.260
Your handstands are 
as floppy as your sasakama!

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:23.580
The hell'd you say?!

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.420
Our Shichigahama really is a simpleton.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.090
And our Takase is a barbarian.

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:29.200
All force, no foresight.

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:31.370
No thought to spare for consequences.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:34.760
But he's also a good captain, you know?

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.910
He's the one who created our team

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:39.830
and has kept us going all this time.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:41.970
Our captain is the same way.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:45.970
Takase is the one who got me 
into rhythmic gymnastics.

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:48.940
And he works hard to find new recruits.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:53.010
Shichigahama was so desperate 
to get us more members

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:54.490
that he had us handing out flyers.

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:58.330
Takase is extremely attentive 
in teaching the new recruits.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:01.400
Shichigahama might be an awful teacher...

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.760
but he's the best performer on our team!

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:07.790
Takase is extremely meticulous 
about cleaning after practice!

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:14.170
Yes, that's better.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:18.910
Perfect.

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:21.470
What lovely blossoms.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:43.240
Aren't you glad everyone's getting along?

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.410
I can't believe how much you've changed.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:48.310
You're the one who always used to say,

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:51.590
"Buddying up is for losers 
who can't make it on their own."

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:53.860
What a dark past you have, Shusaku.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:54.710
An embarrassing reminder!

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:57.020
How's your leg doing?

00:10:57.020 --> 00:11:00.280
It gets me through daily life just fine.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:01.220
I see.

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:04.080
Videos have been going up online,

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:07.470
and we're getting some media coverage,

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:10.750
<b><i>The Current State of 
Rhythmic Gymnastics</i></b>

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:12.200
but men's rhythmic gymnastics 
is still far from being an A-list sport.

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.610
Too true.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:18.150
If you'd stayed in the game, 
we might be on top of it right now.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:20.150
You give me too much credit.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.390
I'm not!

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:24.570
A single star performer 
can make a huge difference.

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:27.110
We're making new stars.

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:30.120
If only you hadn't participated
in that competition...

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:33.250
I still think about that from time to time.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:36.380
Lamenting the past won't build us a future.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:39.970
Shida...

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.560
My wife says that a lot.

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:49.290
You know, I've never actually met your wife.

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:51.270
Well, she's just very shy.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:52.330
She exists.

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.520
Oh... really?

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:55.850
Hey!

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:56.920
Here?

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:01.350
Are those guys even hidin'?

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:03.760
I bet they just bailed.

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:07.750
But, man, the school
 sure is creepy at night...

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:09.100
Prime real estate for ghosts.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.670
Wh-Why'd you say that?
Is this school haunted?

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:14.470
I heard somethin' about it once. 
How'd it go again?

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:17.020
The ghost who wanders the halls, Hanako-san....

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:18.640
No, Yuriko-san.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:20.940
Umeko? Suzuko? Takako?

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.340
H-How many of them are there?!

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:24.300
It's all stupid.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.530
Only an idiot would believe
 a story like that.

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:27.340
Right?

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:29.930
Yeah, totally.

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:34.940
Dance
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h<u>along<i></i></u>!

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:38.350
Your fan preference is Ma-chan 
of the Tan-Tan Girls, as I recall.

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:40.100
Yeah, wanna watch with?

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:41.040
No.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:44.280
I don't hold Ma-chan 
in particularly high regard.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:48.450
I guess there's no pleasing some people.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:50.440
Her persona is far too polished.

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:52.240
It lacks authenticity.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.670
Idols are all about the fantasy!

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:59.380
If you ask me, your oh-so-great Nebuta Dream
is way too open about how hard they try.

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:00.190
Grr.

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:03.320
It's Nebuta Dream's aim to form 
a personal connection with their fans.

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:06.410
Idols should reflect the truth of life.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:11.640
The pursuit of flawless beauty 
is anachronistically idealistic.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:14.870
Ma-chan knows that and does it anyway!

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:18.440
Who wants to see girls suffering 
for their art after a long day's work?

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:21.030
Watching them smiling 
and having fun reinvigorates us,

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.780
even if it's just a fantasy!

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:26.220
It seems you view idols 
as a means of pure escapism.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:31.080
I see them as my comrades 
in the daily struggles of life.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:33.170
What? Quit dressin' it up in fancy language.

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:34.920
You just like 'em because they're cute!

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:35.960
Incorrect.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:37.660
You <i>don't</i> think they're cute, then?!

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:40.350
A logical fallacy. 
Your argument is invalid.

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:42.740
So you like yakuza movies, huh?

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:44.860
Yeah, you know. You, too?

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:47.580
I'm in it for the action, personally.

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:49.380
Any flicks you like in particular?

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:51.920
Anything starrin' Bunya.

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:56.300
Oh... I'm not a huge fan of his stuff.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.730
The bad guys always mistreat him,
 and he toughs it out

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:02.510
only to get killed at the end, y'know?

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:04.990
That's what makes 'em so great.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:08.860
If he's such a bad dude, 
why not kill him off at the start?

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:09.280
What?!

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:11.620
And a lot of the time, 
he hides how he feels

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:14.470
all for the girl he likes, right?

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:17.790
I'm not a big fan of that. 
Feels old-fashioned.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:22.050
Beat the bad guys and get the girl 
in a romantic happy ending!

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:25.510
I think <i>that's</i> what makes a great movie.

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:27.260
But a real man—

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:30.010
No, hang in there.

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:31.790
That's what real men do.

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:38.270
I guess a little kid wouldn't 
understand how real men live.

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:40.650
I-I'm no kid!

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:43.860
<b>Library</b>

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:43.860
The library, huh?

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.930
Shichigahama would never cross on red,
even with no cars coming!

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:48.500
When someone asks Takase for directions,

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:50.360
he always guides them to their destination!

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:52.890
Shichigahama always gives up 
his seat for the elderly!

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:55.990
Takase always picks up litter 
and puts it in the trash can!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:56.870
Shichigahama is—

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:57.940
Takase is—

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:03.660
Anyone there?

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:06.420
I figured Tsukidate would come here first.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:11.250
It was Ma-chan's devotion to her public image
as an idol that attracted me to her!

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:13.400
Perhaps she's simply not 
being honest with herself.

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:15.960
There's nothing dishonest 
about Ma-chan's idol spirit!

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:18.210
Are you saying you can't 
believe in an idol unless

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:20.040
they say what they feel every damn second?!

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:22.220
I simply prefer to share in their struggles.

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:24.830
There's no need for idols to show their—

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:27.810
Er, guess we made too much racket.

00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:30.490
We must be the first to—

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:33.390
Huh?

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:34.960
No one here.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:39.200
Hangin' in there is what makes a man!

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.620
You gotta beat the bad guy at the start!

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:45.170
A man should be able to hold back 
for the sake of his sweetheart!

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:48.510
I prefer romantic happy endings!

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:49.910
By the way, Watari-san,

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:52.930
I think you've been a little loud 
for someone playing hide-and-seek!

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:53.930
What the—

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.280
Another bust, huh?

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:02.060
For real, where <i>are</i> those guys?

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:20.080
<b>Sasashichi
Sasa
Kamaboko</b>

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.120
Do you think the captains 
have found anyone at all?

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.130
I'd expect it to be a struggle.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:25.960
Yeah...

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:28.770
Your captain is so weird.

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:30.260
So is yours.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:33.410
Our senpais all have such 
distinct personalities.

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:34.960
Yours, too.

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:36.150
You think?

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:38.390
You're the strangest of the bunch, Mashiro.

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:43.440
I have to wonder if it's a problem for me.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:47.650
Maybe I need more of a personality 
to catch up to the rest of you.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:51.370
Isn't there anything you like 
besides rhythmic gymnastics?

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:54.360
Me? Well... I like playing video games 
and reading dictionaries.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.000
I also really like my mom's gyoza.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:56.960
Boring.

00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:59.790
I kinda like the Tan-Tan Girls...

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:02.000
Though not as much as Onagawa-senpai.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.410
Idt's more just something
 to share with friends.

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:05.740
Boring.

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:07.570
Didn't you do something before this?

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:11.090
Swimming, soccer, baseball...

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:12.850
Hey, just like me.

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:14.050
What, really?

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:17.560
Yeah, I did swimming in kindergarten, 
soccer in elementary school,

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:18.870
and baseball in junior high.

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:20.100
That's exactly like me!

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.950
Hey, why did you stop?

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:24.390
Did you have trouble becoming a regular, too?

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:28.060
I just got bored 'cause it was too easy.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.940
Yeah, figures...

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:33.170
But I found Misa-pon in rhythmic 
gymnastics, and that made it fun.

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:35.370
I had such a hard time catching up.

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.450
And yet you still surpassed me.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:42.200
But you could pass me back at any time.

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:46.740
You aren't fighting with all your heart yet.

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:49.710
Even at this training camp, 
you were different from in junior high.

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:50.880
So were you.

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:54.510
That's what makes you so much fun.

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:55.760
It's why I like you.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:58.090
And I refuse to lose to people I like.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.740
I really do want to soar.

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:19.800
I don't care if I'm cut out for it or not.

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:23.830
Alongside the two of you...

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.370
No!

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:30.190
I'll be good enough to compete with you!

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:32.210
I'm going to learn to soar!

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:36.510
Futaba...

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.140
H-Hush!

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:40.510
Shotaro, we're in the middle
 of hide-and-seek!

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:41.960
They're gonna find us!

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:42.750
We get it, so just calm down.

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:43.640
All right?

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:45.760
L-Let's sit back down...

00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:47.320
Y-Yeah.

00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:48.320
Okay?

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:55.650
Darn it!

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:56.830
We haven't found anyone!

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:58.430
Where <i>are</i> those guys?

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:01.490
Wh-What the heck?

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:03.070
That sounds like Mashiro!

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:04.630
Shotaro! Misato!

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:09.460
Shotaro! Misato! Where are you?

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:11.370
Mashiro!

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:14.130
Mutsu! Ryugamori!

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:14.130
Tsukidate! Onagawa!

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.380
Ominato! Azuma!

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:16.880
Watari! Manager!

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:18.130
Coach Mabuchi!

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:19.260
Coach!

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:23.140
Guys!

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:25.810
Where are you?!

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.190
Wh-Who's there?

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:35.570
Is that you, Mashiro? M-Mutsu?

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:37.550
Y-You don't think...

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:39.160
Think what?!

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:40.820
The ghost who wanders the halls...

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:45.090
Umeko-san.

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:46.530
Or was it Yuriko-san?

00:19:46.530 --> 00:19:48.200
Suzuko-san? Takako-san?

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.950
Matsuko-san? Yumeko-san? Sumiko-san?

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:53.330
Shigeko-san? Shizuko-san? Mayuko-san?

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:56.140
Chiyoko-san? Hanayo-san? Hanako-san?

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:11.610
We can't apologize enough for all the trouble.

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:12.960
Oh, it's nothing.

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:17.370
Huh? What's all this now?

00:20:17.370 --> 00:20:18.990
Oh, is this where you all were?

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:20.000
You guys!

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.820
You mustn't enter this room 
without permission.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:25.700
Oh, the other guard brought us all here.

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:26.680
What?

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:30.660
Man, I guess the guards were really "it."

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:33.660
So who won?

00:20:33.660 --> 00:20:34.370
Who can say?

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:36.880
The greatest-ever setback in my manhood!

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:38.760
I must strive to be better!

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:39.500
At what?

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:41.050
Thanks.

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:43.880
Sorry. We helped ourselves to your tea.

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:44.840
Huh?

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:45.650
Huh?

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:50.880
Oh... the other guard went off 
to look for our teachers, too.

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:52.380
What?

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:56.850
Truth is, I'm the only guard on duty.

00:20:56.850 --> 00:20:57.840
What?

00:22:36.030 --> 00:22:37.380
S-Senpai?

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:40.250
Hey, Senpai.

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:42.390
You're heavy. Really heavy.

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:44.550
Please wake up, Senpai!

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:46.760
Shh!
